<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Other Pretext Features</title>
  <p>
    Let's say we want add a link to simple syllabus.
    Here's how we would do that: 
    <url href="https://sfcollege.simplesyllabus.com/en-US/syllabus-library">
      Link to Sante Fe's simple syllabus
    </url>.
    Let's say we want to add a picture to our lecture.
    Here's how we would do that:
  </p>
    <figure>
        <caption>
            Your figure caption goes here.
        </caption>
        <image source="imgs/SFCollegeLogo.png">
            <shortdescription>
            Your alt text goes here.
            </shortdescription>
        </image>
    </figure>
  <p>
    Let's say there's a youtube video that would be perfect for explaining this topic.
    Here's how we would do that:
  </p>

</section>